  "question_text": "The population of bees in a hive after $t$ weeks is given by $P(t) = a(0.95)^t + b$.\nInitially, there are 2500 bees, and after 2 weeks there are 2383 bees.",
  "has_diagram": false,
  "subparts": [
    {
      "subpart": "a i",
      "stem": "Find the value of $a$.",
      "final_answer": "$a = 1200$",
      "mark_breakdown": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Set up equations using $P(0) = 2500$ and $P(2) = 2383$"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "Solve simultaneously to find $a = 1200$"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$P(t) = a(0.95)^t + b$. Now $P(0) = 2500 \\implies 2500 = a(0.95)^0 + b \\implies a + b = 2500 \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$. And $P(2) = 2383 \\implies 2383 = a(0.95)^2 + b \\implies 0.9025a + b = 2383 \\quad \\text{--- (2)}$. Solving (1) and (2) simultaneously, we find: $a = 1200$.",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Formulate two equations from known values and solve the system.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Substitute $t = 0$: $a(1) + b = 2500$.",
          "Substitute $t = 2$: $a(0.9025) + b = 2383$.",
          "Subtract (2) from (1): $0.0975a = 117 \\implies a = 1200$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Incorrect squaring of 0.95."
      }
    },
    {
